t and benign renal tumors: do IVIM and diffusion kurtosis imaging perform better than DWI? Eur Radiol. 2019;29(12):6930–6939. doi: 10.1007/s00330-019-06240-6. [ DOI ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 17. Notohamiprodjo M, Dietrich O, Horger W, et al. Diffusion tensor imaging (DTI) of the kidney at 3 tesla-feasibility, protocol evaluation and comparison to 1.5 Tesla. Invest Radiol. 2010;45(5):245–254. doi: 10.1097/RLI.0b013e3181d83abc. [ DOI ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 18. Minervini A, Di Cristofano C, Gacci M, et al. Prognostic role of histological necrosis for nonmetastatic clear cell renal cell carcinoma: correlation with pathological features and molecular markers. J Urol. 2008;180(4):1284–1289. doi: 10.1016/j.juro.2008.06.036. [ DOI ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 19. Koh MJ, Lim BJ, Choi KH, Kim YH, Jeong HJ. Renal histologic parameters influencing postoperative renal function in renal cell carcinoma patients. Korean J Pathol. 2013;47(6):557–562. doi: 10.4132/KoreanJPathol.2013.47.6.557. [ DOI ] [ PMC free article ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 20. Huang Y, Chen X, Zhang Z, et al. MRI quantification of non-Gaussian water diffusion in normal human kidney: a diffusional kurtosis imaging study. NMR Biomed. 2015;28(2):154–161. doi: 10.1002/nbm.3235. [ DOI ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 21. Zhang YD, Wu CJ, Wang Q, et al. Comparison of Utility of Histogram Apparent Diffusion Coefficient and R2* for differentiation of low-grade from high-grade clear cell renal cell carcinoma. AJR Am J Roentgenol. 2015;205(2):W193–201. doi: 10.2214/AJR.14.13802. [ DOI ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 22. Reynolds HM, Parameswaran BK, Finnegan ME, et al. Diffusion weighted and dynamic contrast enhanced MRI as an imaging biomarker for stereotactic ablative body radiotherapy (SABR) of primary renal cell carcinoma. PLoS One. 2018;13(8):e0202387. doi: 10.1371/journal.pone.0202387. [ DOI ] [ PMC free article ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 23. Ding Y, Zeng M, Rao S, Chen C, Fu C, Zhou J. 